/-
# `Work.RTOwed` — discharging the owed inputs of `Work.RTInstance.Owed`

This chapter discharges the four inputs that `Submission/Work/RTInstance/NOTES.md` §4 records as
owed, so that the instance `Work.Space.RTData` of `M̂` becomes unconditional:

1. `Work.RTInstance.FoldAnalytic` — the three analytic facts about the delivered fold charts
   `Work.FoldInst.foldChart` (smoothness and isometry of their transitions, and the height bound of
   their images).  Proved in `Work.RTOwed.FoldAnalytic`;
2. `Work.RTInstance.FillData` — the collar/cusp, polar and core charts of the filling pieces on
   `M̂` (the assembly layer of the area `Cusp`);
3. `Work.RTInstance.CrossData` — the transitions between a transported fold chart and a collar
   chart (where `Work.HypModel.polarToUHS_isometry` and the ceiling `Work.Cusp.beta` enter);
4. `Work.RTInstance.GlueHomeo` — the `τ_v` gluing `Work.FoldInst.Tset ≃ₜ ∂(⊔_v [-1,1]² × T_v)`.

## The mathematics of the fold block (§1)

`Work.FoldInst.foldTheta i r = coordPerm i ∘ mobiusKlein (N_F D_r)`.  A transition of two fold
charts is computed *piecewise*: for `y ∈ Dvor i r ∩ Dvor j s` (a piece of the Voronoi cell
decomposition of `X̄ = ZMod 2 × Q̄`), the two chart values are

  `foldTheta i r y = coordPerm i (mobiusKlein (N_F D_r) y)`,   `foldTheta j s y = coordPerm j (mobiusKlein (N_F' D_s') y)`

so the transition equals the Möbius map `mobius (coordPermMat j * (N_j D_s) * (N_i D_r)⁻¹ *
coordPermMat i⁻¹)`: a coordinate permutation is a Möbius transformation of the upper half space
(this file's `coordPermMat`), a Klein action followed by the inverse of an other one composes to a
Möbius transformation (`mobiusKlein_eq_mobius`), and Möbius transformations are `C^∞` isometries of
the upper half space metric (`Work.HypModel.mobius_contDiffOn`, `Work.HypModel.mobius_isometry`).

Every point of the transition source is covered by such a piece, because the two representatives of
a class of `M̄` are related by an element of the *subgroup generated by the tight sides*: for
`x ∈ Dvor i r` one has `γ ∈ Ksub x ↔ ∃ Δ, γ = wallSum i Δ` with the walls in `Δ` tight at `x`
(`Work.FoldInst.Ksub_eq_wallSum`), and acting by `wallSum i Δ` moves the piece `Dvor i r` to
`Dvor i (flipSet r Δ)` (`Work.FoldInst.actX_image_Dvor`).  This is the reduction that makes the
transition analysis finite: only the *pieces* matter, never the pointwise tight structure.

## Conventions

* `E4 = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)`, `I4 = 𝓘(ℝ, E4)`, `Mbar = Work.FoldInst.Mbar`;
* the *height* of a chart value is its coordinate `3`, and all chart values of the fold charts have
  positive height (they lie in `Work.HypModel.upperHalfSpace`);
* `Work.FoldInst.diagKR (signVec g)` is the diagonal `±1` matrix of the Klein sign change `g`,
  a Lorentz matrix whose `4`-th diagonal entry is `1` (`4` is the timelike coordinate).
-/
